WEBVTT

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:03.560
I'm sorry.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.540
Thank you.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:55.560
It was no time to find out the police came

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.520
Metro home

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:43.270
Stop like that.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:52.420
That man is on the phone.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.520
I conked the hornet, but saw that crash coming,

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.930
and I had to jump.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.590
What makes you think he was killed?

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:00.000
The car of his come roaring up, and the gargoyle show

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:08.660
or jumped out and dragged them out of the rink as limp as a wet rag yes metal speaking

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:13.420
hey which one of your men was cool enough to steal brit reed's car what's that what's on the front

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.890
page of the central weren't you in enough trouble letting the green hornet find your place without

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:23.970
stealing that car i didn't know it was reed's car i'll get it out of here before it can be traced

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:30.000
you needn't worry about the hornet he's dead dead what do you mean

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.370
- Good.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.710
Get Reed's car off your hands and we're pretty.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.810
- Right.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.070
The job that Cory brought in yesterday

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.590
belonged to Britt Reed.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:42.550
- Yeah, I know, but--

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.560
- What's been done to it?

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.010
- Nothing, it's still in the shop.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.680
- Hello. - Hello.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.150
Meadows speaking.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.060
Yes, Mr. Meadows, this is Lou.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.530
Don't alter that bike today and it just came in.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:19.610
Let me.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.220
She's so hot it smokes.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.740
Run it over to the junkyard tonight and have them break it up.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.180
- The police commissioner is here, Mr. Reed.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.690
- Oh, send him in.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:49.170
- Commissioner, what can I do for you?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:51.620
- I just want to pin a medal on the Sentinel.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.900
Your tip on the medals at a park will enable us

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.700
to smash the accessory racket right over.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:57.760
- The accessory racket?

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.000
- Sure, these crooked auto parks.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.290
and replace them with inferior articles.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.760
Then they dispose of their own story.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.550
Don't you think there's a connection between this racket

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.050
and the outfit that are stealing cars?

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.010
- Sure there is.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.540
The small fry we've caught either can't or won't

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.320
give us a lead to the higher up.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:14.790
Maybe it's the Green Hornet himself.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:15.930
- No.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:19.390
- What do you know about the Green Hornet, Miss Kate?

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.960
- Well, nothing, but I don't think he's a criminal.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.850
He's had a hand in breaking up every one of these rackets.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.070
- The district attorney thinks

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.710
he's just clearing away competition.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:30.000
After all, he has the case.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:34.540
couple of murders to his credit that's not been proved he's helped the police in every instance

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:42.080
and as a reward this paper puts a price on his head all right but when i catch your bandit boyfriend

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.180
i'm going to charge you with being an accessory you can quote me as giving the sentinel credit for

00:07:47.180 --> 00:08:00.000
smashing the accessory racket thanks i'll do it bye bye bye they got a line on some of the men that stole your car

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.330
- All right, Michael, let's have it.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.430
- I was checking the junkyards, like you told me,

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.410
and at a place over on the east side,

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.570
what do you think I saw?

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.370
- Well, come on, come on, this is no guessing game.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.200
- It was one of the fellas that lifted your bus off the lot.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.620
- You sure? - Sure, I'm sure.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.270
Of course, he's not there now.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:16.470
He was just driving away when I spotted him.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.730
- Well, let's go take a look at that junkyard.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:30.000
- Sure. - When do you find out?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.270
Everything's quiet at the junkyard.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:34.270
The police haven't connected us with the Meadows Auto Park.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:34.960
Good.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:47.110
- What can I do for you?

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:54.170
- I'm looking for a motor that would do in a power boat.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:57.950
- I guess I can fix you up.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:58.550
- Jake!

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.260
These gents are looking for a motor, show them what we've got.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.520
All right, right over here.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:11.230
Well, they didn't connect this yard with the parking lot, huh?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:17.240
Well, anyway, Reed's given us a chance for that job that Chief ordered.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:18.630
What are you guys doing here?

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.840
Pipe down, Slim.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.160
Two birds that just came in are newspaper men.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.510
Young fellas, Britt Reed.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.800
Heard his own to the Sentinel.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.470
Well, there they are.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.830
Look them over, maybe they'll find something there you can use.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.360
Give me that list of numbers.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:49.260
Why pick my place for your dirty work?

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:54.920
I don't like those kind of accidents.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.640
You'll have an accident you like less if you don't obey orders.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:58.680
Why you.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.830
-suffering snakes. -Wait a minute, Michael.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.310
Hey, Jake.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.340
Wait a minute.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:56.560
This one ought to be alright if the cylinders aren't scored.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.450
This is a junkyard, not a showroom.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.000
You've got to take them as you find them.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.890
- Can't you find what you want?

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.050
- No, they all seem to be in pretty bad shape.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:05.250
- Well, take a look at this one.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.280
- Practically new.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.330
You mothering blackguard.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:42.980
I won't pay that gun, it was just an accident.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:45.040
Well, it sure picked a fine place to happen.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.180
Oh, I'm sorry, men.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:48.200
I don't know how that brick got up there.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.330
Well, nobody was searched, so forget it.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.350
We better tip Meadows at the junkyard to spot her.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:55.450
Our whole works will be spotted if we don't stop reading.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.610
Next time, I'll use a gun.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:58.870
How many men you got working here?

00:12:58.870 --> 00:12:59.920
Just me and Jake.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.920
I guess you haven't got anything here we can use.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:47.120
- Where's Meadows?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:47.940
- In the office.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:53.660
- What's wrong?

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:54.500
- Gladys.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.540
- Did you read that was no accident?

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.140
It was attempted murder.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.310
- You're right, Axford.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.000
Only you didn't get a bullet in your back

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.880
that gun of yours but we're going to get them job with the police you and I are in the newspaper

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:17.530
business but reason part of the junkyard he was out there looking for his car he wouldn't find

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:22.350
anything it's still here but we try to get him and miss what do you mean miss we try to read to

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:28.040
the junkyard no my car was there commissioner there's no doubt the artist connected to the

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:30.000
other rackets in some way get him to me

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:30.980
that spotted the place.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.890
I'll send Axford along to identify the man in case you catch him.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:37.120
The bigger part of it was suspicious,

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:38.780
but Reed just took it as an accident.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:40.960
It's no fault of yours, the whole thing wasn't bungled.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.250
We can't send Reed's car out there now.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.070
Drop it in a river.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.790
We can't drive that far through the streets

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.930
with a big prowl car in town on the lookout for it.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:51.200
It's got to be destroyed.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:54.870
Put a time bomb in it.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:09.250
Oxford has gone with the police, Mr. Britt.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.050
Well, we must get back before he returns.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.430
The Green Hornet will hunt Mr. Meadows?

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.430
I'm convinced that garage is the headquarters

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.040
for the car-stealing racket.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.240
Meadows must face the Green Hornet tonight.

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.410
- Mom's ready, boss.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.850
- What time is she set for?

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:04.910
- Exactly 11:00.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:06.550
Just gives me plenty of time to get the car

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:07.550
to that vacant lot.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.040
- Keep her here a little while.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:09.860
- What for?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.040
Why not run around now?

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.380
- If you keep her on that vacant lot too long,

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:21.560
the police may find her before 11:00.

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:22.280
- What's your motor?

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:35.860
Wait here.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:37.750
Hold it here a little longer.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:38.930
I'll tell you when to go.

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.330
All right, Mr. Meadows.

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:59.760
Oh, your voice.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:03.270
- I want some information concerning the car-stealing racket. - Car-stealing?

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:06.910
Yes. I happen to know you're a member of the crime syndicate in this town.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:09.690
You're a director of the crooked accessories stores.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.860
You're the real owner of Slim's Junkyard.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.580
We even have a shop here in this building to alter stolen cars.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.940
I can give the police enough information to send you to the pen for 20 years.

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:21.380
- What do you want? - The name of the big boss. Back at this crime ring.

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:24.970
I'll give you one minute to talk, Meadows.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.360
Six minutes till that bomb cracks off.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.070
That's cutting it pretty fine.

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:30.000
Run around, Mary.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:31.600
Meadows says to wait.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.370
Not me, I'm taking her out.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:35.900
All right, time's up.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:36.970
I don't know his name.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.200
I can show you how you can reach him.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:40.950
Come this way.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.450
All right, but no tricks.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:50.200
Move!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:40.370
Meadows, put him in Brookridge's car.
